## Screens & components annotated (all 8 routes)

- **Header** (every screen): `nav.home`, `search.query` (input, controls `threads.list`), `nav.new-thread`, `nav.profile`, `nav.logout`, `nav.login`, `nav.register`
- **Sidebar** (Home, Category): `browse.filters` region with sort actions (`browse.filters.trending/recent/hot`, state `threads.filter`), `nav.categories` collection (items keyed by category slug), `stats.*` observables
- **HomePage / CategoryPage**: `threads.list` collection, `threads.heading` / `search.summary` observables (linked to `threads.filter` / `search.query`), `category.title`/`.description`, empty states
- **ThreadCard** (shared): per-item title link (`<list>.item.<thread-id>`, nav → `thread.detail`) plus `.upvote`, `.upvotes`, `.author`, `.replies`, `.views`
- **ThreadPage**: `thread.detail` region (`thread.upvote/.upvotes/.title/.content/.author/.reply-count/.view-count`), `reply.form` region (`reply.content`, `reply.submit` controls `thread.replies`), `thread.replies` collection via **ReplyCard** (item id on the content paragraph, `.upvote/.upvotes/.author`)
- **NewThreadPage**: `new-thread.form`; category select with `data-semtag-options` built from the same `categories.map` that renders the `SelectItem`s (`new-thread.category.option.<id>`); title input + live char-counter sharing state key `new-thread.title`; content, cancel, submit
- **Login / Register / NotFound**: form regions, field inputs, submit actions, cross-links

## Id namespaces

`nav.*`, `search.*`, `browse.filters.*`, `stats.*`, `threads.*`, `category.*`, `thread.*` (incl. `thread.replies.item.*`), `reply.*`, `new-thread.*`, `login.*`, `register.*`, `profile.*`, `error.*`

## Design notes

- Same thread in multiple lists: `ThreadCard` takes a `semtagCollectionId` prop (the one permitted prop-widening); each page scopes item ids (`threads.list.item.*` vs `profile.threads.item.*`), and emits **no** attributes if the prop is absent, per spec §8. Item keys are stable entity ids (`thread-3`, `reply-2`, `tech`), never indexes.
- **Not folded**: profile interest badges — hinted as a single `profile.interests` observable instead of a collection (no per-item controls; interest strings aren't stable slugs).
- **Left unhinted**: per-card category badge (reachable via sidebar), timestamps/avatars, decorative icons, toast notifications.

